>ADACHI KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new"  format="epo"><addressbook><name>AOKI MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook> </applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARIMOTO NOZOMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITA HAYATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRONICS CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUGE SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ADACHI, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AOKI, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARIMOTO, NOZOMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITA, HAYATO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRONICS CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUGE, SHINJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ADACHI KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AOKI MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARIMOTO NOZOMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITA HAYATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUGE SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ADACHI, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AOKI, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARIMOTO, NOZOMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITA, HAYATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUGE, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A stainless steel plate for a shadow mask having the following elemental composition in weight: chromium (Cr): 9 to 20 wt %, carbon (C): 0.15 wt % or less, manganese (Mn): 0 to 1.0 wt %, titanium (Ti): 0 to 0.2 wt %, silica (Si) 0 to 1.0 wt %, aluminum (Al): 0 to 1.0 wt %, balance: iron (Fe) and inevitable impurities, wherein the contents of phosphorus (P) and sulfur (S) in said inevitable impurities satisfy P: 0.05 wt % or less and S: 0.03 wt % or less, respectively; and a stainless steel plate for a shadow mask which is obtained by subjecting a stainless steel plate having the above-defined elemental composition to a cold rolling or shape straightening and subjecting the resulting steel plate to an annealing wherein the maximum temperature of the plate is 550 to 650 DEG C. The stainless steel plate has a coefficient of thermal expansion less than that of low carbon steel, is inexpensive compared to the invar alloy, exhibits a reduced plastic deformation at a high temperature and has a high strength which is satisfactory for a shadow mask to be used under a high tension. The stainless steel plate exhibits also excellent etching characteristics.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une tôle en acier inoxydable pour masque perforé ayant la composition élémentaire en poids suivante: chrome (Cr): 9 à 20 % en poids; carbone (C): au maximum 0,15 % en poids; manganèse (Mn): 0 à 1,0 % en poids; titane (Ti): 0 à 0,2 % en poids; silice (Si): 0 à 1,0 % en poids; aluminium (Al): 0 à 1,0 % en poids; le reste étant constitué de fer (Fe) et d'inévitables impuretés. Dans ces impuretés, les teneurs satisfaisantes en phosphore (P) et en soufre (S) sont, pour P: au maximum 0,05 % en poids, et pour S: au maximum 0,03 % en poids. On obtient une tôle en acier inoxydable pour masque perforé en soumettant une tôle en acier inoxydable ayant la composition élémentaire précitée à un laminage à froid ou un redressement de forme, le résultat obtenu étant ensuite soumis à un recuit, la température maximale de la tôle se situant entre 550  DEG  et 650  DEG C. La tôle en acier inoxydable, dont le coefficient de dilatation thermique est inférieur à celui d'un acier à faible teneur en carbone, est peu coûteuse par rapport à l'alliage invar; elle offre une déformation plastique réduite à haute température et possède une résistance élevée satisfaisante pour un masque perforé à utiliser sous une tension élevée. La tôle en acier inoxydable présente également d'excellentes caractéristiques de gravure.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>